                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 183,
                            "last_played": 1780593020
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I played this on my Acer Aspire 16 AI (N25Q20) with an Intel Core Ultra 5 226V, 16GB LPDDR5X, and the Intel Arc 130V GPU. Game was installed on a MicroSD Card, running Windows 11, and played with a wired PS5 controller.\n\nThe technical stuff: I was getting 200+ FPS on my laptop's 16\" OLED (2048x1280, 120Hz). However, I couldn't lock the framerate to 120FPS, which is a minor annoyance. The game is tiny (under 2GB).\n\nGameplay wise, it’s a simple 2D platformer with light puzzles. If you've played Limbo, you know the vibe: heavy atmosphere, environmental storytelling, no hand-holding. The background music is good and somber. The story is fine but short.\n\nI finished two endings (didn't bother going for the other endings and all the achievements).",
